{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01E6JBL5xdnynLkJAbqQUnLo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils/moreutils verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test a specification-driven code generation pipeline, not ship utilities.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). cmd/ packages hold per-utility implementations and differential tests. pkg/sys, pkg/format, pkg/testutils provide shared infrastructure. Magefiles drive the orchestrator.\n\n**Implementation state**: Most releases through 12.1 are partially or fully implemented. Release 13.0 has df implemented; dir, vdir, and dircolors remain. Releases 14.0 and 15.0 are entirely unstarted.\n\n**Current release focus**: Release 13.0 is the earliest incomplete release with ready requirements. Only `srd109-dircolors` has R-items in \"ready\" state (R1.1–R1.4, R2.1–R2.5, R3.1–R3.5 — 15 total). dir and vdir SRDs are not in requirement_states.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 13.0 → srd109-dircolors is the earliest ready work. 15 requirements at max 4 per task = 4 tasks. No contract task needed — cmd/ main packages have no exported types (package_contracts only lists pkg/ packages). All tasks modify the same files, so they chain sequentially.\n\n## Weight Budget Arithmetic\n\nAssuming default weight 1 for all srd109-dircolors requirements (requirements.yaml not accessible; no evidence of non-default weights):\n\n- Task 0: R1.1(w=1) + R1.2(w=1) + R1.3(w=1) + R1.4(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 1: R2.1(w=1) + R2.2(w=1) + R2.3(w=1) + R2.4(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 2: R2.5(w=1) + R3.1(w=1) + R3.2(w=1) + R3.3(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 3: R3.4(w=1) + R3.5(w=1) = 2 ≤ 4 ✓\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/dircolors: implement srd109 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd109-dircolors.yaml (full SRD -- read all requirements R1.1 through R3.5 for overall design context)\n      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler pattern)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests API)\n      - cmd/printenv/main.go (reference cmd/ implementation pattern for a simple utility)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/dircolors/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: dircolors utility -- main entry point, argument parsing, and R1 group implementation\n      - path: cmd/dircolors/dircolors_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests covering R1.1 through R1.4\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd109 R1.1 -- read the SRD for the exact requirement text and acceptance criteria\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd109 R1.2 -- read the SRD for the exact requirement text and acceptance criteria\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd109 R1.3 -- read the SRD for the exact requirement text and acceptance criteria\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd109 R1.4 -- read the SRD for the exact requirement text and acceptance criteria\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per project convention\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use testutils.BuildBinary and testutils.RunDiffTests for differential testing\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Reference binary is gdircolors via exec.LookPath; t.Skip if not found\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Set LC_ALL=C in test environment per project convention\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/dircolors/main.go compiles with go build -o bin/dircolors ./cmd/dircolors/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/dircolors/ passes with no warnings\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/dircolors/ -count=1 pas